{
  "case_id": "2005-04-885",
  "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you tell us how often States are creditors in bankruptcies around the country? Do you have any idea?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (William E. Thro, Esq.)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves a conflict between two constitutional values. On the one hand, Congress has the sovereign power to make laws which apply to everyone, including the States. On the other hand, the States have sovereign immunity from all aspects of suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ohio",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is some information to that effect in the amicus brief of Ohio and every other State of the Union, Justice O'Connor, but my recollection is that the States are creditors in probably the majority of bankruptcies around the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Tell me, if you're -- if you're right -- let's suppose you're right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Thro",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Traditionally, in rem jurisdiction has a couple of characteristics. One is, it is -- it is everyone against the world. It binds -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Lewis",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- if the States are permitted to opt out of the collective bankruptcy process, and they're permitted to disregard Federal preference statutes with impunity, it will have a negative effect on the bankruptcy process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Souter: Assuming that's so, for sovereign immunity purposes, why should it make a difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if you lose on that, the whole section 106 would probably fall."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. LEWIS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We believe, obviously, Congress had the right to abrogate sovereign immunity -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How is there an informed waiver if the argument is over the authority to abrogate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. LEWIS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, I believe, because this Court has recognized, in Gardner versus New Jersey, that if a State files a proof of claim, it constitutes a waiver, that the State had to have to been informed, it had to know that the actual conduct of filing a proof of claim would have a consequence of a waiver."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you lose on the abrogation notion, and the Court holds that there is no authority in Congress to abrogate sovereign immunity, still the bankruptcy code codifies what is, across the board, the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the motion to dismiss was filed, as recognized by the Petitioner in their brief"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask a question on another subject, just talking for a minute about your in rem theory of the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. THRO",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question presented is whether or not Congress may use the Article 1 Bankruptcy Clause to abrogate sovereign immunity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2005-04-885",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b59102bfdd6e1c2fd49a87232f9930d6bb7d9a66dc5f7594d8897d4d9f38ac5b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b59102bfdd6e-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the question you've presented, Mr. Thro, but it was the same question that was presented to us in Hood."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
